data guarantee_probe_corpus_charter_note: String = "STAGE 1a SLICE 1 OF THE GUARANTEE SPINE (roadmap node ladder-probe-corpus): the landed wall controls from the THREE MERGED PRs gunbc#7519 (call-label-and-surplus), gunbc#7484 (method-established-surface + declared-conformance-ground-fragment), and gunbc#7485 (InferToEval self-grounding frontier) migrated onto gunbc.guarantee_measurement identities — MIGRATE, never duplicate beside the dark-suite originals. gunbc#7555 (InferToTranslate underived-refusal) is OPEN on main and introduces NO path/class/probe identities here — that lane lands its own registry rows with executing evidence when it merges. Each migrated row carries a GuaranteeClassId, GuaranteePathId, and GuaranteeProbeId; receipts name subject_revision, harness_revision, and probe_set_digest per the Stage-0 schema. guarantee_probe_dark_suite_dispositions names each Rust dark-suite witness retained until gap-analysis sec 11 item 9 finite classification — enrolled .dag probes are the floor authority; Rust copies are explicitly dispositioned, not silently parallel. This slice owns the identity registry, canonical probe ordering, and the census-to-observation bridge for the v1 compile path. v2 InferToEval executing evidence joins the registry from src/v2/test/claim/infer_self_grounding_wall_test.dag (frontier value-red and derived-green receipt joins). No disposition, no rung, no claims carrier — those arrive with ladder-claims-carrier. gunbc#7847 (call-missing-and-duplicate-wall, roadmap node rn_EXUHLON5V24YU7Z4XLJFWEZO33, duplicate-label slice) added call_duplicate_red_probe/call_duplicate_green_probe to the SAME call_label_surplus_class as #7519's mislabel/surplus rows — one seam (direct_call_shape_diags), a third refusal mode on it, not a new class. Its Rust dark-suite original is call_shape_duplicate_wall_witness, dispositioned below alongside call_shape_wall_witness."

data guarantee_probe_corpus_execution_status_note: String = "THIS REGISTRY'S WITNESSES DO NOT RUN IN CI, AND EVERY RUNG DERIVED FROM THEM MUST BE READ THROUGH THAT (measured 2026-08-22; gap analysis section 11 item 23). The required floor DISCOVERS a witness file declaring live_tree_disposition = ReadsLiveTree and then DECLINES it before the fold — v2.workflow.required_floor RequiredFloorDisposition DeclinedLiveTree, reported as declined_live, 830 identities on run 32553487573. Every carrier that executes this registry declares exactly that, TRUTHFULLY: compile_dag_diagnostic_census resolves its synthetic source against build_module_path_index_from_witness_roots, which walks the live checkout, and the witnesses filesystem_read their harness sources besides. Five carriers and 100 identities of guarantee evidence sit in that arm: test.claim.guarantee_probe_corpus_witness (50), test.claim.sole_constructor_completeness_audit_probe (26), v2.test.claim.infer_self_grounding_wall_test (12), test.claim.compile_diagnostic_census_witness (8), test.claim.optional_cast_wall_witness (4). DO NOT REPAIR THIS BY RETYPING A DECLARATION. The declarations are correct; a SubstrateInputsOnly relabel would be a fabricated fact about a live-tree read and would corrupt affected-set selection eligibility, which is the question live_tree_disposition actually owns. The specimen that proves the arm is a stale PREDICTION rather than a capability limit: test.claim.match_exhaustiveness_coproduct_witness calls the SAME builtin, declares SubstrateInputsOnly, and executes and passes on the floor today — same host call, opposite declaration, opposite fate, and that mis-declaration is currently the only reason any census-compiling probe runs at all. DISSOLVES when the DeclinedLiveTree arm is deleted at the root, which required_floor's own header already stages and prices (run 32345970386, 626/783 passing under execution); that deletion is sequenced behind the merge queue and was UNOWNED as of 2026-08-22."

data guarantee_probe_corpus_path_scope_note: String = "TWO LANDED PATHS IN THE CANONICAL REGISTRY: v1-compile-rust is subject_grain SyntheticProgram, acceptance_boundary CompileAccept, realization_target EmittedTarget { language: rust } — the path compile_diagnostic_census measures. v2-infer-eval is the same subject grain with acceptance_boundary InferToEval and realization_target InterpreterRealization — the path gunbc#7485's GroundingNotDerived frontier diagnostic lives on. A receipt keyed to one path must not claim coverage the other measures (DESIGN 4b minimum-across-paths discipline)."

data guarantee_probe_corpus_probe_order_note: String = "CANONICAL PROBE ORDERING OBLIGATION (probe_set_digest note): guarantee_probe_ids lists the slice-1 MIGRATED probes in stable lexicographic order by branded id string. Callers must not re-sort; the roster order here IS the probe-set digest authority for this stage."

data guarantee_probe_corpus_revision_note: String = "subject_revision and harness_revision are REQUIRED on every receipt as MeasurementRevision (GitRevision | ContentFingerprint). build_v1_compile_receipt and build_v2_infer_eval_receipt take a path-typed probe row and derive probe_set_digest from row.probe only (single-probe execution in slice 1). Until the baseline stage supplies anchor git commits, witness fixtures mint ContentFingerprint revisions from measured content: synthetic_program_subject_revision fingerprints compiled source text; synthetic_infer_eval_subject_revision_from_node fingerprints the executed Node fixture via v2.std.node.content_hash; v1_compile_harness_revision and v2_infer_eval_harness_revision fingerprint filesystem_read harness source material (v1_compile_harness_source_paths / v2_infer_eval_harness_source_paths) plus the registry row's ProbeExpectation — never symbol-name spines or prose scope notes. dissolve-on ladder-baseline stage naming real GitRevision subject_revision/harness_revision commits."

fn synthetic_program_subject_revision(source: String) -> MeasurementRevision {
  ContentFingerprint { digest: content_hash_atom(value: source as NonEmptyStr) }
}

fn synthetic_infer_eval_subject_revision(subject_material: NonEmptyStr) -> MeasurementRevision {
  ContentFingerprint {
    digest: content_hash_tagged_structural(
      tag: "v2-infer-eval-subject-v1" as NonEmptyStr,
      payload: content_hash_atom(value: subject_material),
    ),
  }
}

fn synthetic_program_harness_revision(probe: GuaranteeProbeId, harness_material: NonEmptyStr) -> MeasurementRevision {
  ContentFingerprint {
    digest: content_hash_tagged_structural(
      tag: "guarantee-probe-harness-v1" as NonEmptyStr,
      payload: content_hash_combine_structural(
        left: content_hash_atom(value: probe as NonEmptyStr),
        right: content_hash_atom(value: harness_material),
      ),
    ),
  }
}

data v1_compile_rust_path_id: GuaranteePathId = "v1-compile-rust" as GuaranteePathId
data v2_infer_eval_path_id: GuaranteePathId = "v2-infer-eval" as GuaranteePathId

fn v1_compile_rust_path() -> GuaranteePath {
  GuaranteePath {
    id: v1_compile_rust_path_id,
    subject_grain: SyntheticProgram,
    acceptance_boundary: CompileAccept,
    realization_target: EmittedTarget { language: "rust" as GuaranteeTargetName },
  }
}

fn v2_infer_eval_path() -> GuaranteePath {
  GuaranteePath {
    id: v2_infer_eval_path_id,
    subject_grain: SyntheticProgram,
    acceptance_boundary: InferToEval,
    realization_target: InterpreterRealization,
  }
}

fn guarantee_probe_paths() -> List<GuaranteePath> {
  [v1_compile_rust_path(), v2_infer_eval_path()]
}

