// THE SIX UNENROLLED FLOOR CLASSES (gap analysis sec 11 item 10 + the parse-separator and
// v2-exemption rows beside it). Each was measured ONCE by hand and cited in a sec 1c Evidence
// cell; nothing in the corpus re-ran the measurement, so the rung was honest about 2026-08-01
// and silent about today. These class ids exist so the measurement executes on every floor run
// (DESIGN 4b meta-obligation 4). FOUR of them are BELOW-FLOOR HOLES, not walls: their probes
// declare ExpectSilentAcceptanceHole, which is a pinned defect and NOT a passing control -- read
// the variant's own note before treating a green here as a guarantee.
data floor_closed_match_exhaustiveness_class: GuaranteeClassId = "floor-closed-match-exhaustiveness" as GuaranteeClassId
data floor_declared_conformance_v2_exemption_class: GuaranteeClassId = "floor-declared-conformance-v2-module-exemption" as GuaranteeClassId
data floor_field_through_generics_class: GuaranteeClassId = "floor-field-through-generics" as GuaranteeClassId
data floor_generic_instantiation_class: GuaranteeClassId = "floor-generic-instantiation-inhabitance" as GuaranteeClassId
data floor_parse_list_separator_class: GuaranteeClassId = "floor-parse-list-separator" as GuaranteeClassId
data floor_record_field_completeness_class: GuaranteeClassId = "floor-record-field-completeness" as GuaranteeClassId

data floor_class_seam_note: String = "WHY floor-declared-conformance-v2-module-exemption IS A SEPARATE CLASS FROM declared-conformance-ground-fragment, and not a nickname for it (DESIGN 3). The judgment is the same judgment -- a value must inhabit its declared type -- but the gap analysis row for it records that the class has AT LEAST TWO SEAMS and that closing one must never be read as closing the class. declared-conformance-ground-fragment measures the RETURN/data seam, which refuses in every module. This class measures the DIRECT-CALL ARGUMENT seam, which v1.compiler.04_infer module_skips_direct_call_arg_check switches OFF for every caller module whose name begins with v2., i.e. for the entire active v2 corpus. One class id per seam is what keeps a green on the first from reading as coverage of the second. The enumeration is NOT closed: a record-literal FIELD seam is measured below floor in ordinary non-v2 modules (gunbc#8865) and has no probe here, so this corpus covers two of at least three seams."

fn guarantee_probe_class_ids() -> List<GuaranteeClassId> {
  [
    bare_none_field_admission_class,
    call_label_surplus_class,
    declared_conformance_ground_class,
    floor_closed_match_exhaustiveness_class,
    floor_declared_conformance_v2_exemption_class,
    floor_field_through_generics_class,
    floor_generic_instantiation_class,
    floor_parse_list_separator_class,
    floor_record_field_completeness_class,
    method_established_surface_class,
    sole_constructor_cross_module_class,
    v2_self_grounding_frontier_class,
  ]
}

